source: crates/instrukt-cli/tests/cases/harness.rs
expression: help
---
Attributed commits and reclaimed build output in the acting agent's authoring worktree

Usage: instrukt repo <COMMAND>

Commands:
  commit   Commit as the acting agent: its configured git author, a `Session:` trailer when a
           runtime's session variable is set, `Human-Involved:` always, and `Todo:` or
           `Planned-Todo:` with --todo. Outside an agent session the commit is the git user's own.
           In an adopted project it takes the author's review-routing choice
           (`general/policy/commits`): --review, or --exempt <BASIS>, which records the commit's
           exemption once it exists. Prints the commit's id
  reclaim  Reclaim the declared regenerable output of the worktree this session's todo assignment
           records; it takes no location. Prints each path removed and each declared path left with
           why
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version
